    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><dateline><date when="1945-11-24">November 24,
                        1945</date></dateline><salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3352"
                            type="person">Miss Watson</rs>:</salute>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to <rs ref="#L10879" type="letter">your request of November 21</rs>,
                    concerning <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3353" type="person">Mrs. Margaret
                        Blumenfeld Plaut</rs> I would like to give you the following
                    information:</p>
                <p>I have known <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3353" type="person">Mrs. Plaut</rs>
                    already in <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__736" type="place">Europe</rs> and have
                    then met her often in this country from <date when="1938">1938</date> on. <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__3353" type="person">Mrs. Plaut</rs> has been and
                    still is one of the most efficient volunteer social workers of the SELFHELP OF
                    EMIGRES FROM CENTRAL <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__736" type="place">EUROPE</rs>,
                    Inc. of which organization I am the Chairman. She is excellent in interviewing
                    people, has full understanding for their problems, a clear point of view and
                    consequently always finds a way in rehabilitating refugees or placing them on
                    the right job. Besides that she has creative abilities. She composes the
                    pamphlet for Selfhelp, edits reports and appeals.</p>
                <p>For the last three years she acts as Executive Secretary of the COOPERATIVE
                    RESIDENCE CLUB, a home for elderly refugees, working in close cooperation with
                    Selfhelp. She is doing this work independently and very efficiently.</p>
                <p><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3353" type="person">Mrs. Plaut</rs> stems from a
                    highly cultured family. Both her educational background and her intellectual
                    standard qualify her for whatever position you might secure for her. I know very
                    few people whom I would recommend as strongly as I do recommend <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__3353" type="person">Mrs. Plaut</rs>.</p>
                <closer><salute>Sincerely yours,</salute><signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928"
                            type="person">Paul Tillich</rs>
                        <lb/>Professor at Union Theological Seminary, <rs
                            ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York City</rs></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
